          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "S0-10 (and S0-10-features.txt:2) classifies the spec grep's 30 lines as '21 feature arrays, 8 `name =` keys, 1 comment'. Re-running the same `git grep` at HEAD and classifying each line by its TOML shape gives 21 feature arrays, 7 `name =` keys and 2 comments: crates/aprender-test/Cargo.toml:82 is a comment (`# APR-MONO: in-tree sibling, ... [lib] name = \"trueno\")`) that merely mentions `name =`, beside the genuine comment crates/aprender-graph/Cargo.toml:64. The feature-array count G-1 depends on (21) is correct; the 8/1 split is not."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
